---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import { timeline, languages, expertise } from "../data/site";
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Serhat Akkuş — twenty years in software, eight leading teams, now tutoring developers and building products under ParionTech."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="About"
    title="Twenty years in, still curious."
    lede="I have been writing software professionally since before I finished my degree — more than twenty years, most of it in Java, most of it building enterprise systems for the financial sector. I have been a developer, a lead developer, a team leader and an architect, and these days I spend most of my week teaching."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <p>
          I studied Computer Engineering at Yıldız Technical University and started working as a
          developer before I graduated in January 2005. Nearly all of the two decades since have been
          spent in the financial sector — large enterprise applications in Java, the kind of systems
          where a rounding error is a serious incident and the code outlives the team that wrote it.
        </p>
        <p>
          The first years were about learning the craft properly: object-oriented design, design
          patterns that earn their complexity, relational data modelling, and a great deal of SQL and
          PL/SQL. Then I moved into leading — lead developer, team leader, software architect — and
          did that for eight-plus years. That is where I learned the part nobody teaches you in
          engineering school: the hard problem is almost never the code. It is getting five people to
          agree on what "done" means, deciding which technical debt to keep, and knowing when the
          honest answer is "we built the wrong thing."
        </p>
        <p>
          In 2019 I started{" "}
          <a href="https://pariontech.com" rel="noopener" target="_blank">ParionTech</a>{" "}
          to build the things I wanted to build properly. And over the last few years I have moved
          most of my time into tutoring — Java, algorithms and Python, mostly with computer science
          students at universities in Europe and the US. Teaching one-to-one turns out to be the most
          direct way to pass on twenty years of expensive lessons.
        </p>

        <h2>How I think about software</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Improvement belongs inside development, not after it.</strong> The idea behind
          ParionTech is that refactoring, testing and cleanup are not a phase you schedule when there
          is time. There is never time. They are part of how the thing gets built.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Design patterns are vocabulary, not architecture.</strong> Twenty years of
          enterprise Java taught me that the patterns are worth knowing precisely so you can tell
          when you do not need one. Most over-engineering I have seen came from someone applying a
          pattern to prove they knew it.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Boring technology wins.</strong> Java, Spring and a well-modelled relational
          database have carried systems I wrote fifteen years ago that are still running. I would
          rather spend my thinking on the actual problem than on the framework.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>The data model is the real design.</strong> In financial systems especially, get
          the schema and the domain model right and the application code becomes almost boring. Get
          them wrong and no amount of clean code above will save you.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Path</p>
      <ol class="timeline">
        {
          timeline.map((entry) => (
            <li class="timeline__item">
              <p class="timeline__period">{entry.period}</p>
              <div class="timeline__body">
                <h3 class="timeline__title">{entry.title}</h3>
                <p class="timeline__org">{entry.org}</p>
                <p class="timeline__text">{entry.body}</p>
              </div>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">What I work with</p>
      <dl class="stack">
        {
          expertise.map((g) => (
            <div class="stack__group">
              <dt class="stack__label">{g.group}</dt>
              <dd class="stack__items">
                <ul class="tags">
                  {g.items.map((i) => (
                    <li class="tag tag--solid">{i}</li>
                  ))}
                </ul>
              </dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">Spoken languages</p>
      <ul class="langs">
        {
          languages.map((l) => (
            <li class="langs__item">
              <span class="langs__name">{l.name}</span>
              <span class="langs__level">{l.level}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>

      <p class="about__cta">
        <a class="arrow-link" href="/contact/">Get in touch</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .stack {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-m);
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .stack__group {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-xs);
    padding-block: var(--space-s);
    border-block-end: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  @media (min-width: 44rem) {
    .stack__group {
      grid-template-columns: 13rem 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-m);
      align-items: start;
    }
  }

  .stack__label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    padding-block-start: 0.2rem;
  }

  .stack__items {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .stack .tag--solid {
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
    color: var(--text);
    border-color: var(--border-strong);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    padding: 0.35em 0.8em;
  }

  .timeline {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin-block-start: var(--space-m);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-m);
  }

  .timeline__item {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2xs);
    padding-inline-start: var(--space-m);
    border-inline-start: 1px solid var(--border);
    position: relative;
  }

  .timeline__item::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset-inline-start: -4.5px;
    top: 0.55rem;
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent);
  }

  @media (min-width: 44rem) {
    .timeline__item {
      grid-template-columns: 9.5rem 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-m);
      align-items: start;
    }
  }

  .timeline__period {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--text-faint);
    padding-block-start: 0.15rem;
  }

  .timeline__title {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }

  .timeline__org {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-block-start: 0.1rem;
  }

  .timeline__text {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-2xs);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .langs {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin-block-start: var(--space-s);
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
  }

  .langs__item {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-s);
    padding-block: var(--space-xs);
    border-block-end: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .langs__name {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    font-weight: 620;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .langs__level {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    text-align: end;
  }

  .about__cta {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-l);
  }
</style>
